    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [ ] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Question\n\nWhile working on my code I found out that `mini.comment` doesn’t comment lines in Verilog (.v), SystemVerilog (.sv), and Arduino (.ino) files. Instead, it throws the error:\r\n```lua\r\nmini.comment() object commentstring is empty.\r\n```\r\nI was able to fix it by explicitly setting `commentstring` in the pre hook like this:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.comment\").setup({\r\n    hooks = {\r\n        pre = function()\r\n            local ft = vim.bo.filetype\r\n            if ft == \"verilog\" or ft == \"systemverilog\" or ft == \"arduino\" then\r\n                vim.bo.commentstring = \"// %s\"\r\n            end\r\n        end,\r\n    },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n**Not sure if this is a bug, a missing default configuration, or a dependency issue.** Should this be handled internally by `mini.comment`, or is it expected that users manually configure `commentstring` for these file types?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.comment</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While working on my code I found out that <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.comment</code> doesn’t comment lines in Verilog (.v), SystemVerilog (.sv), and Arduino (.ino) files. Instead, it throws the error:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"mini.comment() object commentstring is empty.\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">mini</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">comment</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">object</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">commentstring</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">is</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">empty</span>.</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was able to fix it by explicitly setting <code class=\"notranslate\">commentstring</code> in the pre hook like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require(&quot;mini.comment&quot;).setup({\n    hooks = {\n        pre = function()\n            local ft = vim.bo.filetype\n            if ft == &quot;verilog&quot; or ft == &quot;systemverilog&quot; or ft == &quot;arduino&quot; then\n                vim.bo.commentstring = &quot;// %s&quot;\n            end\n        end,\n    },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.comment<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">hooks</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n        <span class=\"pl-en\">pre</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n            <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">ft</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">filetype</span>\n            <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">ft</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>verilog<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">ft</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>systemverilog<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">ft</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>arduino<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n                <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">commentstring</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>// %s<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n            <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    },\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Not sure if this is a bug, a missing default configuration, or a dependency issue.</strong> Should this be handled internally by <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.comment</code>, or is it expected that users manually configure <code class=\"notranslate\">commentstring</code> for these file types?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.comment\nQuestion\nWhile working on my code I found out that mini.comment doesn’t comment lines in Verilog (.v), SystemVerilog (.sv), and Arduino (.ino) files. Instead, it throws the error:\nmini.comment() object commentstring is empty.\nI was able to fix it by explicitly setting commentstring in the pre hook like this:\nrequire(\"mini.comment\").setup({\n    hooks = {\n        pre = function()\n            local ft = vim.bo.filetype\n            if ft == \"verilog\" or ft == \"systemverilog\" or ft == \"arduino\" then\n                vim.bo.commentstring = \"// %s\"\n            end\n        end,\n    },\n})\nNot sure if this is a bug, a missing default configuration, or a dependency issue. Should this be handled internally by mini.comment, or is it expected that users manually configure commentstring for these file types?",
