                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, this is correct. Inferring comment structure from 'commentstring' is a [documented behavior](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b9440aed49221f0dbcaf481937b73a61f9ef32bf/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14).\r\n\r\nOne small thing I'd change is to use `vim.bo.commentstring` instead of `vim.opt_local.commentstring`. As the latter is probably going to be deprecated in the future.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, this is correct. Inferring comment structure from 'commentstring' is a <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b9440aed49221f0dbcaf481937b73a61f9ef32bf/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14\">documented behavior</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One small thing I'd change is to use <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.bo.commentstring</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.opt_local.commentstring</code>. As the latter is probably going to be deprecated in the future.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, this is correct. Inferring comment structure from 'commentstring' is a documented behavior.\nOne small thing I'd change is to use vim.bo.commentstring instead of vim.opt_local.commentstring. As the latter is probably going to be deprecated in the future.",
